{"resourceIdentifier":"3715","resourceName":"TAIHE COUNTY BIOGAS POWER GENERATION AND ORGANIC FERTILIZER PROJECT","description":"Taihe County Biogas Power Generation and Organic Fertilizer Project is located at ShuangXing Village, Shuang fu Town, Taihe County, Fuyang City, Anhui Province, China.This project builds a new livestock and poultry manure management system and collects organic wastes such as manure from many farms to produce biogas power generation and organic fertilizer. Fermentation raw materials are managed by unified collection and transportation. Agricultural waste resources (ie, livestock and poultry wastes in this project) undergo pretreatment and anaerobic fermentation, and the generated biogas is desulfurized and then enters the generator to generate electricity. The waste heat of the generator is used to increase the temperature of the material in the homogenization tank and the fermentation tank. The mud produced by anaerobic fermentation is transported to the nearby farmland through the pipeline network to form an organic ecological cycle industry. The residue is used to produce solid organic fertilizer. The electricity generated is fed into the East China grid, reducing methane and other greenhouse gas emissions. It also avoids the CO2 emissions generated by the power generation process corresponding to the replacement of electricity, thereby achieving greenhouse gas emission reduction.The project activity will reduce GHG in the atmosphere through avoiding methane emissions from anaerobic treatment of manure. The project adopts a 10-year fixed crediting period, It is estimated that 62,834 tCO2e emission reductions will be generated annually and total emission reductions are 628,338 t CO2e in the crediting period.","location":{"latitude":33.316378,"longitude":115.605277},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-10-12","endExclusive":"2022-11-12","endInclusive":"2022-11-11"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_I